# E-1117: Let $f(z)$ be an entire function which is not a monomial. Let $\nu(r)$ count the number of $z$ with $\lvert z\rvert=r$ such that $\lvert f(z)\rvert=\max_{\lvert z\rvert=r}\lvert f(z)\rvert$. (This is a finite quantity if $f$ is not a monomial.) Is it possible for\[\limsup \nu(r)=\infty?\]Is it possible for\[\liminf \nu(r)=\infty?\]
